# adv360 notes for Void Linux

Testing my Advantage360 Professional on Linux, I have had mixed results with many keys. `evtest` has been able to detect many of these while X11 cannot. I don't particularly understand why.

## [Consumer Controls](https://zmk.dev/docs/keymaps/list-of-keycodes#consumer-controls)

|     Name      | Works? |
| ------------- | ------ |
| C_MEDIA_HOME  | No.    |
| C_MEDIA_CD    | No.    |

## [Applications (Launch)](https://zmk.dev/docs/keymaps/list-of-keycodes#applications-launch)

| Name | Works? |
| --------------------- | ----------------- |
| C_AL_AUDIO_BROWSER    | No.               |
| C_AL_CALCULATOR       | Yes!              |
| C_AC_DESKTOP_SHOW_ALL_WINDOWS  | As "Launch". |
| C_AL_DOCUMENTS        | No.               |
| C_AL_FILE_BROWSER     | As "Browser".     |
| C_AL_KEYBOARD_LAYOUT  | No.               |
| C_AL_MY_COMPUTER      | As "Browser".     |
| C_AL_SCREEN_SAVER     | As "Pause".       |
| C_AL_TASK_MANAGER     | No.               |
| C_KBIA_NEXT           | No.               |
| C_NEXT                | As "Media Next".  |
| C_RESET               | Yes (careful!)    |
| C_POWER               | Yes!              |
| C_SLEEP               | Yes!              |
| CLEAR_AGAIN           | No.               |
| F24                   | No.               |
| K_APP                 | Yes!              |
| K_CALC                | No.               |
| K_FORWARD             | No.               |
| K_NEXT                | No.               |

## [Input Assist](https://zmk.dev/docs/keymaps/list-of-keycodes#input-assist)

|             Name               | Works? |
| ------------------------------ | ------ |
| C_KEYBOARD_INPUT_ASSIST_ACCEPT | No.    |
| C_KEYBOARD_INPUT_ASSIST_CANCEL | No.    |
